  "context_pill": "Section 115BAC Default Tax Regime & Section 87A Rebate",
  "example_summary": "Computation of tax liability for Mr. Mahesh (Resident Individual, age 32) with ₹ 11,00,000 total income for A.Y. 2026-27 under Section 115BAC.",
  "source_provision": "### Statutory Framework: Section 115BAC & Section 87A Rebate\n\n| Statutory Provision | Target Assessee | Operative Slab / Limit | Statutory Tax Rate / Treatment |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Section 115BAC(1A)** | Individual / HUF / AOP / BOI / AJP | Up to ₹ 4,00,000 | **Nil** |\n| **Section 115BAC(1A)** | Individual / HUF / AOP / BOI / AJP | ₹ 4,00,001 to ₹ 8,00,000 | **5%** |\n| **Section 115BAC(1A)** | Individual / HUF / AOP / BOI / AJP | ₹ 8,00,001 to ₹ 12,00,000 | **10%** |\n| **Section 115BAC(1A)** | Individual / HUF / AOP / BOI / AJP | ₹ 12,00,001 to ₹ 16,00,000 | **15%** |\n| **Section 115BAC(1A)** | Individual / HUF / AOP / BOI / AJP | ₹ 16,00,001 to ₹ 20,00,000 | **20%** |\n| **Section 115BAC(1A)** | Individual / HUF / AOP / BOI / AJP | ₹ 20,00,001 to ₹ 24,00,000 | **25%** |\n| **Section 115BAC(1A)** | Individual / HUF / AOP / BOI / AJP | Above ₹ 24,00,000 | **30%** |\n| **Section 87A Proviso** | Resident Individual | Total Income $\\le$ Prescribed Statutory Limit | **100% Tax Payable or Max Statutory Rebate Limit (whichever is lower)** |\n\n#### Key Statutory Rules & Eligibility Conditions\n\n- **Default Application**: Section 115BAC applies automatically as the default tax regime unless the assessee exercises an option to opt out under Section 115BAC(6).\n\n- **Resident Individual Rebate**: Section 87A provides complete relief from tax liability where the Total Income of a resident individual does not exceed the statutory threshold limit under the default regime.\n\n- **Marginal Relief Mechanism**: Where Total Income slightly exceeds the eligibility threshold under Section 87A, marginal relief limits tax to the amount of income exceeding that threshold.\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> Section 87A rebate under Section 115BAC is available **only to Resident Individuals**. Non-residents, HUFs, AOPs, and BOIs are strictly ineligible for rebate under Section 87A regardless of total income.",
